00:24:01,100 --> 00:24:04,367
- A most endearing wish.

525
00:24:05,333 --> 00:24:06,800
- So really, by this time,

526
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:08,267
a kid had thrown a chicken,

527
00:24:08,267 --> 00:24:12,067
while an infertile couple
had looked at a store.

528
00:24:12,067 --> 00:24:13,733
- I have my own,
private fertility clinic

529
00:24:13,733 --> 00:24:14,900
in back, baby.

530
00:24:16,633 --> 00:24:18,300
- All right, I've seen enough.

531
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:20,633
I could be a sport about this.

532
00:24:20,633 --> 00:24:22,533
If you're really
Merlin, prove it.

533
00:24:22,533 --> 00:24:23,900
Show me something.

534
00:24:23,900 --> 00:24:25,900
As they say, knock my socks off.

535
00:24:25,900 --> 00:24:27,367
(laughs)

536
00:24:27,367 --> 00:24:28,300
- You have no socks.

537
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:30,300
- We don't give demonstrations.

538
00:24:30,300 --> 00:24:31,333
- Sure you don't.

539
00:24:31,333 --> 00:24:32,800
(Servo mocks the line)

540
00:24:32,800 --> 00:24:34,267
Listen to me, Obi Wan.

541
00:24:34,267 --> 00:24:36,000
Either you give me something
to write home about,

542
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:39,100
or your quaint little
shop is history.

543
00:24:39,100 --> 00:24:40,467
- Jonathan, let's just go.

544
00:24:40,467 --> 00:24:41,733
- I'm being a jerk, honey.

545
00:24:41,733 --> 00:24:43,133
- Did you hear me, old man?

546
00:24:43,133 --> 00:24:44,867
Do you know who I am?

547
00:24:44,867 --> 00:24:47,333
I am the supreme being.

548
00:24:47,333 --> 00:24:48,833
- Clapton?

549
00:24:48,833 --> 00:24:51,067
- I chew places like this up
and spit them into the toilet.

550
00:24:51,067 --> 00:24:51,900
(Mike, Servo, and Crow laugh)

551
00:24:51,900 --> 00:24:53,167
- Why?

552
00:24:53,167 --> 00:24:54,367
- So I'm gonna give
you one last chance.

553
00:24:54,367 --> 00:24:55,700
You prove to me
that you're Merlin,

554
00:24:55,700 --> 00:24:59,033
the great sorcerer,
or get off the pot.

555
00:24:59,033 --> 00:25:00,933
- For God sakes,
Jonathan, just drop it.

556
00:25:00,933 --> 00:25:02,433
Leave these kind people alone.

557
00:25:02,433 --> 00:25:06,167
- Otherwise I won't continue
to not have your children.

558
00:25:06,167 --> 00:25:07,000
- Dear...

559
00:25:08,033 --> 00:25:10,700
Why don't you give him the book?

560
00:25:12,167 --> 00:25:13,433
- The book?

561
00:25:13,433 --> 00:25:14,833
- Yes, dear.

562
00:25:14,833 --> 00:25:16,600
The book.

563
00:25:16,600 --> 00:25:18,267
Your book.

564
00:25:18,267 --> 00:25:19,867
- Button your robe.

565
00:25:21,133 --> 00:25:23,133
- What's going on?

566
00:25:23,133 --> 00:25:24,767
- One of our dwarves died.

567
00:25:24,767 --> 00:25:26,100
- Mister Cooper.

568
00:25:27,267 --> 00:25:29,400
I may have something for
you that will provide

569
00:25:29,400 --> 00:25:31,667
the proof you seek.

570
00:25:31,667 --> 00:25:33,400
- [Jonathan] Oh yeah?

571
00:25:34,967 --> 00:25:37,700
- It's a pie from
Baker's Square.

572
00:25:39,667 --> 00:25:40,933
- Looks like an old book.

573
00:25:40,933 --> 00:25:42,167
- Do do do do do do!

574
00:25:42,167 --> 00:25:45,367
- [Merlin] Oh, that
it is, Mister Cooper.

575
00:25:45,367 --> 00:25:47,067
It's a book of magic.

576
00:25:47,067 --> 00:25:48,533
- With a pop-o-matic.

577
00:25:48,533 --> 00:25:50,100
- My own compilation of

578
00:25:50,100 --> 00:25:52,100
spells and incantations.

579
00:25:52,967 --> 00:25:55,233
- More talk of magic?

580
00:25:55,233 --> 00:25:56,833
I told you the only kind

581
00:25:56,833 --> 00:25:59,100
of magic I believe in
is the magic I have

582
00:25:59,100 --> 00:26:01,100
in these fingers
to make this place

583
00:26:01,100 --> 00:26:03,533
(snaps fingers) disappear.

584
00:26:03,533 --> 00:26:06,533
- Mister Cooper, if you would
just take this book home

585
00:26:06,533 --> 00:26:10,133
and read through it, I
assure you, you will be

586
00:26:10,133 --> 00:26:12,333
thoroughly satisfied.

587
00:26:12,333 --> 00:26:14,400
- [Merlin] I'm sure you
will find that it makes

588
00:26:14,400 --> 00:26:15,233
- Do do do do do do...

589
00:26:15,233 --> 00:26:16,733
- good reading.

590
00:26:16,733 --> 00:26:19,267
- It's on the Oprah list.

591
00:26:19,267 --> 00:26:22,733
- All right, you've sparked
my interest, old man.

592
00:26:22,733 --> 00:26:24,433
I'll look through it.

593
00:26:24,433 --> 00:26:27,100
And you'll trust me
to bring it back?

594
00:26:27,100 --> 00:26:27,933
- [Merlin] Why, certainly.

595
00:26:27,933 --> 00:26:29,367
Oh, Missus Cooper.

596
00:26:29,367 --> 00:26:30,300
- You're fine!

597
00:26:30,300 --> 00:26:32,700
- Please, keep the stone.

598
00:26:32,700 --> 00:26:34,567
- [Madeline] Oh, no, I couldn't.

599
00:26:34,567 --> 00:26:36,633
- Dear, it's a gift.

600
00:26:36,633 --> 00:26:39,667
- Have some slightly
used dress shields, too.

601
00:26:39,667 --> 00:26:41,033
- Thank you.

602
00:26:41,033 --> 00:26:42,300
- You're welcome!

603
00:26:42,300 --> 00:26:43,233
- You're welcome.

604
00:26:43,233 --> 00:26:44,967
- Come on, let's get outta here.

605
00:26:44,967 --> 00:26:46,567
I'm sure the
compilations of a mad man

606
00:26:46,567 --> 00:26:48,867
will make good reading.

607
00:26:48,867 --> 00:26:50,367
- [Merlin] Oh,
and Mister Cooper.

608
00:26:50,367 --> 00:26:51,767
- You're welcome.

609
00:26:51,767 --> 00:26:53,700
- A few words of caution.

610
00:26:53,700 --> 00:26:57,533
If you decide to dabble
with any of my spells,

611
00:26:57,533 --> 00:26:58,900
for whatever reason.

612
00:26:58,900 --> 00:26:59,733
- You're welcome!

613
00:26:59,733 --> 00:27:00,933
- Be sure not to toy

614
00:27:00,933 --> 00:27:02,100
- (laughs) Do it again!

615
00:27:02,100 --> 00:27:04,033
- with any that
aren't entirely there.

616
00:27:04,033 --> 00:27:06,267
- You insulting my sperm count?

617
00:27:06,267 --> 00:27:09,033
- I'm afraid that
over the years,

618
00:27:10,200 --> 00:27:12,400
some of the pages
have become brittle.

619
00:27:12,400 --> 00:27:13,700
- Like the missus, here.

620
00:27:13,700 --> 00:27:15,533
- And sections have...

621
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:18,733
broken off.

622
00:27:18,733 --> 00:27:20,900
- Again like the missus here.

623
00:27:20,900 --> 00:27:24,000
- So please, Mister Cooper,

624
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:25,600
heed my words.

625
00:27:25,600 --> 00:27:27,933
- Munch my shorts.

626
00:27:27,933 --> 00:27:29,600
- For your own sake.

627
00:27:30,800 --> 00:27:33,833
- Look, my reviews have
destroyed whole cities.

628
00:27:33,833 --> 00:27:36,767
(doors clang shut)

629
00:27:45,633 --> 00:27:48,233
- Yeah, so anyway, Mike, it's
clear that niche reviewing

630
00:27:48,233 --> 00:27:49,600
is the wave of the future.

631
00:27:49,600 --> 00:27:51,033
- Mm-hmm.

632
00:27:51,033 --> 00:27:52,233
- The ugly guy in the movie
reviews novelty stores

633
00:27:52,233 --> 00:27:54,967
and CD strip malls,
and he's famous!

634
00:27:54,967 --> 00:27:57,433
- Yeah, so we figured why
not review each other?

635
00:27:57,433 --> 00:27:58,867
- Yeah.
(Servo laughs)

636
00:27:58,867 --> 00:28:00,667
- It'll tell the world
about our delightful selves,

637
00:28:00,667 --> 00:28:03,300
which needs to happen,
and we become famous.

638
00:28:03,300 --> 00:28:04,667
- I'll go first.

639
00:28:04,667 --> 00:28:05,600
(clears throat)

640
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:07,500
From the moment I saw Tom Servo,

641
00:28:07,500 --> 00:28:09,300
I was taken with his gay,

642
00:28:09,300 --> 00:28:11,267
even naughty bright red color.

643
00:28:11,267 --> 00:28:12,467
And the unexpected,

644
00:28:12,467 --> 00:28:14,067
clear Pyrex dome.

645
00:28:14,067 --> 00:28:15,867
The little dangly arms, though

646
00:28:15,867 --> 00:28:17,933
the function was unclear,

647
00:28:17,933 --> 00:28:19,400
added to the lighthearted

648
00:28:19,400 --> 00:28:20,967
feel of the experience.

649
00:28:20,967 --> 00:28:21,933
Flawless?

650
00:28:21,933 --> 00:28:23,133
No.

651
00:28:23,133 --> 00:28:25,533
But I recommend this
Tom Servo for children,

652
00:28:25,533 --> 00:28:28,467
and anyone looking for a
bare bones kinda robot.

653
00:28:28,467 --> 00:28:30,233
There you go.

654
00:28:30,233 --> 00:28:31,067
- Huh.

655
00:28:31,067 --> 00:28:31,933
My turn?

656
00:28:31,933 --> 00:28:32,800
Good.

657
00:28:32,800 --> 00:28:33,767
(clears throat)

658
00:28:33,767 --> 00:28:35,167
Everyone's talking about the new

659
00:28:35,167 --> 00:28:37,333
Crow T. Robot out
on Highway Six.

660
00:28:37,333 --> 00:28:40,067
Insouciant, ecclectic,
it seems to promise

661
00:28:40,067 --> 00:28:41,400
a kind of excitement.

662
00:28:41,400 --> 00:28:42,900
Yet the overall effect becomes

663
00:28:42,900 --> 00:28:44,900
rather more garish than fun,

664
00:28:44,900 --> 00:28:48,500
and I left feeling
altogether empty and sad.

665
00:28:48,500 --> 00:28:50,967
- Well, seems like you
guys are on your way

666
00:28:50,967 --> 00:28:52,233
with the whole niche
reviewing thing, so...

667
00:28:52,233 --> 00:28:54,300
- Hey, hold on, Mike,
hold on, hold on.

668
00:28:54,300 --> 00:28:56,267
My second visit to Tom Servo

669
00:28:56,267 --> 00:28:57,933
was even a greater
disappointment.

670
00:28:57,933 --> 00:28:59,533
Loud and overpriced.

671
00:28:59,533 --> 00:29:01,100
- What?

672
00:29:01,100 --> 00:29:02,733
- There was a thick, oily
film coating every surface,

673
00:29:02,733 --> 00:29:05,467
and I can only hope I escaped
with no serious disease.

674
00:29:05,467 --> 00:29:07,767
- If my readers
responses are any guide,

675
00:29:07,767 --> 00:29:10,300
the Crow T. Robot era
is coming to a close.

676
00:29:10,300 --> 00:29:13,567
This poorly conceived
disaster is revealed now as

677
00:29:13,567 --> 00:29:16,833
a spindly testament to
poor taste and nausea.

678
00:29:16,833 --> 00:29:19,600
- The verdict is in, and
the world was not awaiting

679
00:29:19,600 --> 00:29:21,433
a chubby, pompous eunuch!

680
00:29:21,433 --> 00:29:22,667
- What do you mean, chubby?

681
00:29:22,667 --> 00:29:23,467
- Uh, we'll let these
guys sort it out, we'll

682
00:29:23,467 --> 00:29:24,300
be right back.

683
00:29:24,300 --> 00:29:25,167
- I'll give you chubby.

684
00:29:25,167 --> 00:29:26,000
Goodbye, Crow T. Robot.

685
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:27,400
Your ghastly memory.

686
00:29:27,400 --> 00:29:28,333
- Pathetic, ugly,
overbearing and stupid...

687
00:29:28,333 --> 00:29:29,267
- still pollutes my mind.

688
00:29:29,267 --> 00:29:32,167
(upbeat pop music)

689
00:29:38,833 --> 00:29:42,733
- [Grandpa] And so,
Mister Cooper took
Merlin's book home...

690
00:29:42,733 --> 00:29:43,667
- Wait a minute.

691
00:29:43,667 --> 00:29:45,000
What did Madeline wish for?

692
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:45,833
(Mike and Robots laugh)
- What?

693
00:29:45,833 --> 00:29:46,667
- What do you think?

694
00:29:46,667 --> 00:29:48,033
- I don't know.

695
00:29:48,033 --> 00:29:49,900
- You'll figure it out.

696
00:29:49,900 --> 00:29:51,733
- Are you Susie's boy?

697
00:29:54,667 --> 00:29:57,667
- Well, let's go
make love, I guess.

698
00:30:00,300 --> 00:30:02,167
- I spoke to Doctor Collins.

699
00:30:02,167 --> 00:30:03,100
- Oh yeah?

700
00:30:03,100 --> 00:30:04,033
What'd that quack have to say?

701
00:30:04,033 --> 00:30:05,100
- He blamed your weiner.

702
00:30:05,100 --> 00:30:06,300
- Nothing.

703
00:30:06,300 --> 00:30:08,533
Nothing that would concern you.

704
00:30:08,533 --> 00:30:10,433
- Oh, for Pete's sake, Madeline.

705
00:30:10,433 --> 00:30:11,800
- Why is it so difficult for you

706
00:30:11,800 --> 00:30:13,833
to show a little
compassion once in awhile?

707
00:30:13,833 --> 00:30:15,367
Or to be nice?

708
00:30:15,367 --> 00:30:18,000
My God, just getting along
is a major accomplishment.

709
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:18,800
- Yeah.

710
00:30:18,800 --> 00:30:19,633
- Whew.

711
00:30:20,733 --> 00:30:23,567
If she had a store,
I'd crush her.

712
00:30:24,867 --> 00:30:28,633
- All right, how do you
get outta this thing?

713
00:30:28,633 --> 00:30:30,467
- Well, it would
appear that I, too,

714
00:30:30,467 --> 00:30:32,467
have succumbed to
the old man's charm,

715
00:30:32,467 --> 00:30:35,633
for I hold in my hand
a book of spells.

716
00:30:35,633 --> 00:30:38,767
Merlin's book of spells,
which no less promises

717
00:30:38,767 --> 00:30:42,567
to make me a true
believer in magic.

718
00:30:42,567 --> 00:30:44,367
Although I must admit
the mere thought

719
00:30:44,367 --> 00:30:47,233
of such a thing being
real is intriguing.

720
00:30:47,233 --> 00:30:49,100
- That's your
garage door opener.

721
00:30:49,100 --> 00:30:50,900
- Oh, a warning.

722
00:30:50,900 --> 00:30:54,667
Ye beware who layeth
sight on the pages within.

723
00:30:54,667 --> 00:30:56,033
(laughs)

724
00:30:56,033 --> 00:30:57,300
Nice touch.

725
00:30:57,300 --> 00:30:58,267
- But I probably
should get around

726
00:30:58,267 --> 00:31:00,067
to destroying Kozlak's hardware.

727
00:31:00,067 --> 00:31:01,367
- Must be a fuse.

728
00:31:03,133 --> 00:31:04,067
- Whew!

729
00:31:04,067 --> 00:31:06,167
Finally got outta that car.

730
00:31:06,167 --> 00:31:08,400
- Okay, what do we have, here?

731
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:10,867
- Merlin's light summer recipes.

732
00:31:10,867 --> 00:31:14,400
- Contents: Spells, Love Potion.

733
00:31:14,400 --> 00:31:15,467
Worthless.

734
00:31:15,467 --> 00:31:17,133
Teleportation...

735
00:31:17,133 --> 00:31:18,567
Hm, Rejuvenation.

736
00:31:18,567 --> 00:31:21,733
Ah, yes, we must
stay young and vital.

737
00:31:21,733 --> 00:31:24,033
- (laughs) What's his deal?

738
00:31:24,033 --> 00:31:28,267
- What kind of mind spends
hours writing this crap?

739
00:31:29,333 --> 00:31:30,933
Look at this gibberish.

740
00:31:30,933 --> 00:31:32,033
Typically, in Latin.

741
00:31:32,033 --> 00:31:33,200
- Dumbass language.

742
00:31:33,200 --> 00:31:34,667
- Who was it that first
instilled a belief

743
00:31:34,667 --> 00:31:37,767
that words, perhaps
in their purest form,

744
00:31:37,767 --> 00:31:40,400
could actually
command the elements?

745
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:41,633
- Uh, Bob Hope?

746
00:31:41,633 --> 00:31:45,267
- Take this spell, for
example, to propel away.

747
00:31:45,267 --> 00:31:47,733
Derisera, oh!

748
00:31:48,933 --> 00:31:51,067
- The rug feels soft on my back,

749
00:31:51,067 --> 00:31:52,333
and yet one can't help wondering

750
00:31:52,333 --> 00:31:56,100
whether extra padding
might not be called for.

751
00:31:59,467 --> 00:32:01,933
- That's what I get
for screwing around.

752
00:32:01,933 --> 00:32:03,700
Oh, hey, Miff.

753
00:32:03,700 --> 00:32:04,500
- I have ear mites.

754
00:32:04,500 --> 00:32:05,733
(cat meows)

755
00:32:05,733 --> 00:32:07,500
- All right, debating
whether to continue

756
00:32:07,500 --> 00:32:09,900
on with this foolishness,
Jonathan Cooper

757
00:32:09,900 --> 00:32:13,100
decides to play wizard
in Name That Spell.

758
00:32:13,100 --> 00:32:14,700
- I name it Fred.

759
00:32:14,700 --> 00:32:17,433
- Here's a good
one: To Levitate.

760
00:32:17,433 --> 00:32:21,500
Arisadare, Arisadare!

761
00:32:21,500 --> 00:32:23,600
(laughs)

762
00:32:23,600 --> 00:32:25,967
Look at me, I'm
the wizard, Merlin,

763
00:32:25,967 --> 00:32:27,533
the all-powerful sorcerer!

764
00:32:27,533 --> 00:32:29,867
(cat meows)

765
00:32:31,733 --> 00:32:33,500
- It's time for a
strongly worded review

766
00:32:33,500 --> 00:32:34,933
of my cat, Miffy.

767
00:32:38,533 --> 00:32:40,467
- Doesn't he look like
Judy's husband, Punch?

768
00:32:40,467 --> 00:32:41,867
- Oh yeah, Punch.

769
00:32:41,867 --> 00:32:44,700
- Ooh, To Summon a
Spirit, say three times in

770
00:32:44,700 --> 00:32:47,500
a commanding tone,
Vien-e-chi-Re,

771
00:32:47,500 --> 00:32:50,733
Vien-e-chi-Re, Vien-e-chi-Re.

772
00:32:50,733 --> 00:32:52,033
- Ah, a doratio!

773
00:32:53,433 --> 00:32:56,833
- Ooh, somebody put
tinfoil in the microwave.

774
00:32:56,833 --> 00:32:58,533
(coughs)

775
00:32:58,533 --> 00:32:59,367
(fire flames)

776
00:32:59,367 --> 00:33:00,600
(Servo laughs)

777
00:33:00,600 --> 00:33:03,667
- Channeling the spirit
of a circus freak.

778
00:33:08,933 --> 00:33:11,933
- Now he can return
That arc welder.

779
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:14,800
- Oh, what am I saying?

780
00:33:14,800 --> 00:33:17,567
(dramatic music)

781
00:33:18,667 --> 00:33:20,567
- Oh, thank you, Latin.

782
00:33:25,933 --> 00:33:30,100
- Clearly, Merlin has
brought good into the world.

783
00:33:31,267 --> 00:33:34,033
- Those Altoids are
curiously strong.

784
00:33:35,333 --> 00:33:36,833
(Madeline coughs)

785
00:33:36,833 --> 00:33:38,767
- Ed from next door came
