00:55:42,033 --> 00:55:43,567
- [Dad] Can I play
with it for a minute?

1298
00:55:43,567 --> 00:55:44,400
- Sure.

1299
00:55:44,400 --> 00:55:45,433
- If you give me a beer.

1300
00:55:45,433 --> 00:55:46,633
- Isn't he adorable?

1301
00:55:46,633 --> 00:55:48,267
- Yeah, where'd you
find this thing?

1302
00:55:48,267 --> 00:55:50,500
- Oh, you know that
junk antique store

1303
00:55:50,500 --> 00:55:51,933
off the boulevard?

1304
00:55:51,933 --> 00:55:53,133
- Yeah.

1305
00:55:53,133 --> 00:55:54,700
- I saw it in the window
as I was passing by,

1306
00:55:54,700 --> 00:55:56,933
and I just couldn't resist.

1307
00:55:56,933 --> 00:56:00,400
- Ugh, too many
Seagram's Golden Coolers.

1308
00:56:03,633 --> 00:56:06,667
(telephone rings)

1309
00:56:06,667 --> 00:56:08,933
- '70's house, may I help you?

1310
00:56:08,933 --> 00:56:09,867
- Hello?

1311
00:56:09,867 --> 00:56:12,600
Oh, hello, mother! How are you?

1312
00:56:12,600 --> 00:56:14,433
- You calling from the basement?

1313
00:56:14,433 --> 00:56:15,933
- No, everything's fine.

1314
00:56:15,933 --> 00:56:18,133
Michael's fine, we're all fine.

1315
00:56:18,133 --> 00:56:20,433
Yeah, you enjoying your trip?

1316
00:56:20,433 --> 00:56:23,300
- No, Mom, I don't know why
they took Hazel off the air.

1317
00:56:23,300 --> 00:56:26,700
- Great, great, when
are you coming home?

1318
00:56:26,700 --> 00:56:28,033
- That soon, huh?

1319
00:56:28,033 --> 00:56:29,933
- Okay, three days,
well, call me.

1320
00:56:29,933 --> 00:56:31,333
Call me and let me
know when to pick--

1321
00:56:31,333 --> 00:56:33,233
Now, don't be silly, Mother.

1322
00:56:33,233 --> 00:56:34,567
Look, don't you dare take a cab.

1323
00:56:34,567 --> 00:56:36,300
I'm perfectly capable
to pick you up.

1324
00:56:36,300 --> 00:56:37,567
- What are you,
like 50 pounds now?

1325
00:56:37,567 --> 00:56:38,400
- Good.

1326
00:56:39,533 --> 00:56:42,567
Okay, well, enjoy the
rest of your trip.

1327
00:56:42,567 --> 00:56:46,300
Yeah, okay, I look forward
to seeing you, too.

1328
00:56:46,300 --> 00:56:47,133
Okay.

1329
00:56:47,133 --> 00:56:47,967
- G-goodbye.

1330
00:56:47,967 --> 00:56:48,800
- I will.

1331
00:56:48,800 --> 00:56:49,667
- G-g-goodbye!

1332
00:56:49,667 --> 00:56:50,733
- Bye bye.

1333
00:56:50,733 --> 00:56:53,400
(ominous music)

1334
00:56:54,567 --> 00:56:56,900
- Wow, Mom's youth dew
is so strong it came

1335
00:56:56,900 --> 00:57:00,200
over the phone and
killed the plant.

1336
00:57:00,200 --> 00:57:01,500
- I think he has one of those

1337
00:57:01,500 --> 00:57:03,900
newfangled LaCoste shirts on.

1338
00:57:05,733 --> 00:57:09,667
- Now, Mr. Wilson's doing
nude yard work again.

1339
00:57:12,900 --> 00:57:15,133
- Oh please, since when
has a man ever noticed

1340
00:57:15,133 --> 00:57:16,400
a plant in the house?

1341
00:57:16,400 --> 00:57:20,733
- Oh, that's right,
Moses cursed me.

1342
00:57:23,300 --> 00:57:26,167
- Borgnine's grandson's
really bored by now.

1343
00:57:26,167 --> 00:57:28,100
- He putted around
the kitchen for awhile

1344
00:57:28,100 --> 00:57:30,500
and got himself a cold drink.

1345
00:57:32,933 --> 00:57:34,767
- I wuv you this much.

1346
00:57:37,000 --> 00:57:41,500
- Ah, yep, that first morning
beer is always the best.

1347
00:57:43,267 --> 00:57:46,033
- Working at home, the reality.

1348
00:57:46,033 --> 00:57:49,167
- This is the evil toy
monkey for Polident.

1349
00:57:49,167 --> 00:57:51,833
(ominous music)

1350
00:57:55,033 --> 00:57:58,300
- (in high voice) Oh no!

1351
00:57:58,300 --> 00:58:00,300
- John McEnroe writing
letters of apology

1352
00:58:00,300 --> 00:58:02,167
to various line judges.

1353
00:58:02,167 --> 00:58:04,733
(cymbal rings)

1354
00:58:06,967 --> 00:58:11,133
- It's also a long-range
bug zapper, that's handy.

1355
00:58:12,567 --> 00:58:15,833
- Hm, is that two-hour
Incredible Hulk special

1356
00:58:15,833 --> 00:58:18,433
on tonight or is that tomorrow?

1357
00:58:23,300 --> 00:58:26,067
- Hm, let's see, if I
open another beer now,

1358
00:58:26,067 --> 00:58:28,400
it would save me time later.

1359
00:58:32,967 --> 00:58:35,133
- This place has much
nicer weather than Camelot.

1360
00:58:35,133 --> 00:58:37,133
It never snows at all.

1361
00:58:37,133 --> 00:58:37,967
- Excuse me.

1362
00:58:37,967 --> 00:58:38,800
- Get away from me.

1363
00:58:38,800 --> 00:58:40,000
- I have mace.

1364
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:41,367
- Please, I mean you no harm.

1365
00:58:41,367 --> 00:58:42,633
- Wow.

1366
00:58:42,633 --> 00:58:44,033
- I'm simply trying to
find this toy monkey.

1367
00:58:44,033 --> 00:58:45,633
By chance, have you seen it?

1368
00:58:45,633 --> 00:58:47,100
- Um...

1369
00:58:47,100 --> 00:58:47,933
- That's it.

1370
00:58:47,933 --> 00:58:48,767
Look at the monkey.

1371
00:58:48,767 --> 00:58:50,100
- Actually, yes.

1372
00:58:51,333 --> 00:58:53,567
I'm sorry for the way I behaved.

1373
00:58:53,567 --> 00:58:55,067
- There's no need.

1374
00:58:55,067 --> 00:58:57,633
- It's just that this isn't
a very good neighborhood.

1375
00:58:57,633 --> 00:58:59,767
I mean, you wouldn't
believe the weirdos.

1376
00:58:59,767 --> 00:59:02,433
You just can't be too careful.

1377
00:59:02,433 --> 00:59:04,900
You know, I mean, I know mace
is illegal and everything.

1378
00:59:04,900 --> 00:59:06,133
- Of course, of course.

1379
00:59:06,133 --> 00:59:07,733
I understand.

1380
00:59:07,733 --> 00:59:11,133
But you said you've
seen the monkey?

1381
00:59:11,133 --> 00:59:15,367
- Yes, yesterday this
weird guy brought it in.

1382
00:59:15,367 --> 00:59:17,333
I gave him $5 for it.

1383
00:59:17,333 --> 00:59:18,467
- Do you have it?

1384
00:59:18,467 --> 00:59:20,433
- No, I'm sorry, I don't.

1385
00:59:20,433 --> 00:59:23,333
It sold shortly thereafter.

1386
00:59:23,333 --> 00:59:24,600
- Blast it.

1387
00:59:24,600 --> 00:59:26,133
- Now I've got to
send you to hell.

1388
00:59:26,133 --> 00:59:27,400
- I should be
getting back to work.

1389
00:59:27,400 --> 00:59:30,333
- Please, by chance, do
you have any information

1390
00:59:30,333 --> 00:59:32,567
on the person who bought it?

1391
00:59:32,567 --> 00:59:35,733
- No, I'm sorry, she
paid cash for it.

1392
00:59:36,933 --> 00:59:37,933
- I see.

1393
00:59:37,933 --> 00:59:40,067
- That just lengthens my beard.

1394
00:59:40,067 --> 00:59:41,933
- It was yours?

1395
00:59:41,933 --> 00:59:43,767
- Stolen from my shop.

1396
00:59:43,767 --> 00:59:46,000
- Look, you wanna meet
for a drink later?

1397
00:59:46,000 --> 00:59:47,767
- I hope you find it.

1398
00:59:47,767 --> 00:59:49,300
- I'll find it all right.

1399
00:59:49,300 --> 00:59:51,367
- Have a nice day.

1400
00:59:51,367 --> 00:59:52,200
- Bye bye.

1401
00:59:52,200 --> 00:59:53,300
- Bye.

1402
00:59:53,300 --> 00:59:54,867
- It's kinda sunny.

1403
00:59:54,867 --> 00:59:57,267
He should really wear a slip.

1404
01:00:01,233 --> 01:00:04,333
- Then, the guys with the
receding hair drove a blue car,

1405
01:00:04,333 --> 01:00:06,300
carefully signaling
his turn and pulling

1406
01:00:06,300 --> 01:00:08,367
into a suburban driveway.

1407
01:00:11,300 --> 01:00:12,600
(door creaks)

1408
01:00:12,600 --> 01:00:13,867
(cymbal rings)

1409
01:00:13,867 --> 01:00:14,767
- Oh, I'm sorry, I
thought you said,

1410
01:00:14,767 --> 01:00:16,400
Da na na na da na na na.

1411
01:00:16,400 --> 01:00:17,233
- Michael?

1412
01:00:19,000 --> 01:00:21,267
- I didn't eat him!

1413
01:00:21,267 --> 01:00:22,800
- Michael?

1414
01:00:22,800 --> 01:00:25,467
(ominous music)

1415
01:00:28,367 --> 01:00:31,467
- Max, Yvonne, Bjorn?

1416
01:00:34,200 --> 01:00:36,633
- The view from his hairline.

1417
01:00:39,100 --> 01:00:41,067
- No, the hamper's full!

1418
01:00:46,233 --> 01:00:47,067
- Michael?

1419
01:00:47,067 --> 01:00:48,600
- He's with Elliot.

1420
01:00:51,867 --> 01:00:56,767
- If you don't talk to your
kids about bedspreads who will?

1421
01:00:58,000 --> 01:00:59,667
- Man, I guess I should
quit prowling around my

1422
01:00:59,667 --> 01:01:02,267
neighbor's house and go home.

1423
01:01:02,267 --> 01:01:03,100
- Michael?

1424
01:01:03,100 --> 01:01:03,933
(toy gun blares)

1425
01:01:03,933 --> 01:01:05,000
- Oh!

1426
01:01:05,000 --> 01:01:08,233
- Oh, oh, my heart!
(groans)

1427
01:01:08,233 --> 01:01:10,500
- You scared me to death.

1428
01:01:10,500 --> 01:01:11,767
- Hi, Dad!

1429
01:01:11,767 --> 01:01:16,067
- (laughs) God, give
me a kiss and a hug.

1430
01:01:16,067 --> 01:01:17,333
Where's Sparkle?

1431
01:01:17,333 --> 01:01:18,567
I thought you were
playing with her?

1432
01:01:18,567 --> 01:01:19,967
I put her in the garage
so when I scared you,

1433
01:01:19,967 --> 01:01:21,767
she couldn't make noise.

1434
01:01:21,767 --> 01:01:24,200
- You rascal, you
planned this whole thing?

1435
01:01:24,200 --> 01:01:25,633
- (giggles) Yep.

1436
01:01:25,633 --> 01:01:27,200
- Well, it worked,
you scared me.

1437
01:01:27,200 --> 01:01:29,067
- I think I'll go
let her in now.

1438
01:01:29,067 --> 01:01:30,733
- Okay, go.

1439
01:01:30,733 --> 01:01:33,067
- And grow some hair, son.

1440
01:01:33,067 --> 01:01:35,733
(toy gun beeps)

1441
01:01:37,733 --> 01:01:40,833
- (yawns)
I'm up, I'm up.

1442
01:01:40,833 --> 01:01:43,500
(ominous music)

1443
01:01:44,700 --> 01:01:47,967
- You know, Frampton
really did come alive.

1444
01:01:49,567 --> 01:01:54,533
- Guess I shouldn't have
filled the bowl with vodka.

1445
01:01:55,733 --> 01:01:57,533
- Rock and roll
martian, I guess.

1446
01:01:57,533 --> 01:01:58,500
- Charlotte!

1447
01:02:00,133 --> 01:02:03,300
- I think we must have given
her too much food, son.

1448
01:02:03,300 --> 01:02:05,233
- Yeah, but she was so skinny.

1449
01:02:05,233 --> 01:02:06,467
- Well, she's
supposed to be skinny.

1450
01:02:06,467 --> 01:02:09,233
Fish aren't made
to eat very much.

1451
01:02:09,233 --> 01:02:10,733
- Can we bury her now?

1452
01:02:10,733 --> 01:02:12,833
- Yeah, we can.

1453
01:02:12,833 --> 01:02:17,400
- Son, if you hold the lid
open, we'll bury her at sea.

1454
01:02:20,867 --> 01:02:22,400
- We'll put her right
out front, okay?

1455
01:02:22,400 --> 01:02:24,767
- Next to the 15 turtles.

1456
01:02:24,767 --> 01:02:27,433
Heh, kids.

1457
01:02:30,600 --> 01:02:33,167
- Oh, I'm so sorry
for your loss.

1458
01:02:33,167 --> 01:02:36,100
(upbeat pop music)

1459
01:02:40,733 --> 01:02:42,400
- The Crips move in.

1460
01:02:46,367 --> 01:02:47,233
(brakes groan)

1461
01:02:47,233 --> 01:02:48,233
- Excuse me.

1462
01:02:51,100 --> 01:02:52,233
(evil laughter)

1463
01:02:52,233 --> 01:02:54,033
- Okay, now we're in hell.

1464
01:02:54,033 --> 01:02:55,167
Finally happened.

1465
01:02:55,167 --> 01:02:57,300
- I'm the old pin cushion man,

1466
01:02:57,300 --> 01:02:59,800
the terror of Balloony Land.

1467
01:02:59,800 --> 01:03:03,033
Folks all hate me,
how they hate me.

1468
01:03:03,033 --> 01:03:04,567
- I got Tang and Bugles.

1469
01:03:04,567 --> 01:03:06,133
- Oh hi, MIke.

1470
01:03:06,133 --> 01:03:07,667
- Hi.

1471
01:03:07,667 --> 01:03:11,433
- Just killing time until
video games are invented.

1472
01:03:11,433 --> 01:03:12,667
- So where's your dad?

1473
01:03:12,667 --> 01:03:14,333
(clattering in the distance)

1474
01:03:14,333 --> 01:03:15,233
Never mind.

1475
01:03:15,233 --> 01:03:17,000
- That's so pleasant.

1476
01:03:21,233 --> 01:03:22,900
- Is this outfit too revealing?

1477
01:03:22,900 --> 01:03:23,733
- Hi!

1478
01:03:23,733 --> 01:03:24,567
- Hi.

1479
01:03:24,567 --> 01:03:25,900
- What'd you do?

1480
01:03:25,900 --> 01:03:26,867
- Cut myself.

1481
01:03:26,867 --> 01:03:28,000
- You bit yourself?

1482
01:03:28,000 --> 01:03:29,133
What an idiot!

1483
01:03:29,133 --> 01:03:30,733
- Mr. Goodwrench.

1484
01:03:30,733 --> 01:03:31,800
(knock on door)
- [Pete] You in there, Dave?

1485
01:03:31,800 --> 01:03:33,033
- Yeah?

1486
01:03:33,033 --> 01:03:34,267
- [Pete] Hey, Dave!

1487
01:03:34,267 --> 01:03:35,767
- No Grandma, you
can't come out!

1488
01:03:35,767 --> 01:03:36,767
- Yes, Pete?

1489
01:03:38,167 --> 01:03:40,333
- [Pete] Get out here, I
need some help working on...

1490
01:03:40,333 --> 01:03:41,867
- All right, I'll be right out!

1491
01:03:41,867 --> 01:03:44,200
- Ha ha ha, that's pleasant.

1492
01:03:46,133 --> 01:03:47,367
- What ya need?

1493
01:03:47,367 --> 01:03:48,833
- I gotta time this thing.

1494
01:03:48,833 --> 01:03:50,367
Can you get in and turn it
over a couple of times for me?

1495
01:03:50,367 --> 01:03:51,200
- Sure.

1496
01:03:52,333 --> 01:03:53,400
- I'm benign.

1497
01:03:56,133 --> 01:03:58,133
- Brought to you by LSD.

1498
01:03:59,533 --> 01:04:00,633
(laughter)

1499
01:04:00,633 --> 01:04:02,933
- That's particularly funny.

1500
01:04:04,567 --> 01:04:08,900
- Nobody writes for the
solo cymbal anymore.

1501
01:04:08,900 --> 01:04:10,600
(loud pop)

1502
01:04:10,600 --> 01:04:13,133
(dog whimpers)

1503
01:04:13,133 --> 01:04:14,733
- Remember that kitten, Billy?

1504
01:04:14,733 --> 01:04:16,500
That was nothing
compared to this.

1505
01:04:16,500 --> 01:04:19,067
At least the kitten
went quick, Billy.

1506
01:04:19,067 --> 01:04:22,100
(suspenseful music)

1507
01:04:22,100 --> 01:04:23,867
- I'm just waiting
for firing line.

1508
01:04:23,867 --> 01:04:24,800
- I'll get tough.

1509
01:04:24,800 --> 01:04:26,633
I'll just call his bluff.

1510
01:04:26,633 --> 01:04:28,333
- Oh no, oh no, please no!

1511
01:04:28,333 --> 01:04:30,233
- Just throw me a wet towel.

1512
01:04:30,233 --> 01:04:31,567
I'll do it.

1513
01:04:33,300 --> 01:04:34,567
- One more rep.

1514
01:04:34,567 --> 01:04:36,500
(dog whimpers)

1515
01:04:36,500 --> 01:04:39,033
- Fine, I'll just fashion a
crude mask from dryer hose

1516
01:04:39,033 --> 01:04:41,467
and charcoal briquets.

1517
01:04:41,467 --> 01:04:43,167
- Do it again.

1518
01:04:43,167 --> 01:04:44,333
(engine sputters)

1519
01:04:44,333 --> 01:04:45,567
Hold it.

1520
01:04:45,567 --> 01:04:46,833
I'm not gonna be able
to do it like this,

1521
01:04:46,833 --> 01:04:48,367
not mechanically.

1522
01:04:48,367 --> 01:04:49,900
I'm gonna need my timing light.

1523
01:04:49,900 --> 01:04:51,467
- Why don't you go
extinguish your dog?

1524
01:04:51,467 --> 01:04:52,500
- You wouldn't know where it is,

1525
01:04:52,500 --> 01:04:53,667
would you, old buddy?

1526
01:04:53,667 --> 01:04:55,400
- Uh, it's probably
in my garage.

1527
01:04:55,400 --> 01:04:56,567
You probably left it in there.

1528
01:04:56,567 --> 01:04:57,400
- Uh-huh.

1529
01:04:57,400 --> 01:04:59,067
- Yeah.
(laughs)

1530
01:04:59,067 --> 01:05:00,133
I'll go get it.

1531
01:05:00,133 --> 01:05:02,300
(Mike, Servo, and Crow chuckle)

1532
01:05:02,300 --> 01:05:05,333
- I'm gonna buy an Ann
Gillian poster later.

1533
01:05:05,333 --> 01:05:07,833
(dog whines)

1534
01:05:07,833 --> 01:05:08,767
- Puppy!

1535
01:05:08,767 --> 01:05:11,167
- Back off or my lips get it.

1536
01:05:13,067 --> 01:05:15,667
- Boy, they have a long house.

1537
01:05:15,667 --> 01:05:18,333
(intense music)

1538
01:05:19,500 --> 01:05:21,667
- My AMC Pacer's in there!

1539
01:05:23,867 --> 01:05:26,633
(cymbal rings)

1540
01:05:26,633 --> 01:05:29,233
- But there are funny cartoons.

1541
01:05:32,267 --> 01:05:33,100
- Sparkle?

1542
01:05:34,100 --> 01:05:34,933
Sparkle!

1543
01:05:34,933 --> 01:05:36,533
- Are you done yet?

1544
01:05:38,167 --> 01:05:42,167
- Finish my fine washables,
then I'll douse the fire.

1545
01:05:42,167 --> 01:05:46,200
- Are you chilly, fire,
do you want a light wrap?

1546
01:05:46,200 --> 01:05:49,200
- (coughs) Sparkle?

1547
01:05:50,500 --> 01:05:53,400
- Aw, it melted my leisure suit.

1548
01:05:53,400 --> 01:05:54,233
- Stay inside!

1549
01:05:54,233 --> 01:05:55,067
- Oh!

1550
01:05:55,067 --> 01:05:56,300
Stay here, honey.

1551
01:05:56,300 --> 01:05:58,867
- We're gonna change the
dog's name to Crispy.

1552
01:05:58,867 --> 01:06:00,800
- David, what happened?

1553
