- Don't come, I'm not
worth the trouble.

1884
01:20:50,933 --> 01:20:52,800
- Oh, she is, huh?

1885
01:20:52,800 --> 01:20:54,233
Okay, yeah.

1886
01:20:54,233 --> 01:20:56,800
- Did you tape Robert
Schuler for me?

1887
01:20:56,800 --> 01:20:58,533
- You did, huh?

1888
01:20:58,533 --> 01:21:01,533
Yeah, I'm sure
he'll be surprised.

1889
01:21:01,533 --> 01:21:03,867
Okay, I'll see you in
a little while, yeah.

1890
01:21:03,867 --> 01:21:04,700
Bye bye.

1891
01:21:05,800 --> 01:21:07,033
Hey, Grandma's at the airport.

1892
01:21:07,033 --> 01:21:08,267
She'll be here in
a little while!

1893
01:21:08,267 --> 01:21:09,400
- All right!

1894
01:21:09,400 --> 01:21:10,867
- A few more
minutes without her!

1895
01:21:10,867 --> 01:21:12,367
- Why don't you go make sure
your room is clean, huh?

1896
01:21:12,367 --> 01:21:13,200
- Okay.

1897
01:21:14,633 --> 01:21:16,767
- And put on a clean shirt
while you're at it, will ya?

1898
01:21:16,767 --> 01:21:18,500
- I like this shirt.

1899
01:21:18,500 --> 01:21:20,000
- Michael, that shirt is filthy!

1900
01:21:20,000 --> 01:21:21,233
Will you change it so Grandma
doesn't think I've been

1901
01:21:21,233 --> 01:21:22,833
falling down on the job?

1902
01:21:22,833 --> 01:21:24,000
- Okay.

1903
01:21:24,000 --> 01:21:26,400
- I'll kill another
of your dogs.

1904
01:21:28,567 --> 01:21:31,233
(magical music)

1905
01:21:32,700 --> 01:21:36,200
- Got hit on the cheek
with a tiny meteor.

1906
01:21:39,067 --> 01:21:42,400
- Huh, Borgnine forgot
to write this in.

1907
01:21:43,833 --> 01:21:47,800
- Maybe I can use it as a
bottle opener or something.

1908
01:21:49,267 --> 01:21:53,333
- Grandpa Borgnine, please
no, not another subplot!

1909
01:21:54,500 --> 01:21:57,033
- I need to grow more ear hair.

1910
