Forgive me. Jake Cosgrove.

1920
01:22:23,700 --> 01:22:24,567
Nice to know ya.

1921
01:22:24,567 --> 01:22:25,567
- Merlin.

1922
01:22:25,567 --> 01:22:26,567
- Of course.

1923
01:22:27,700 --> 01:22:30,767
(clears throat) So Merlin...

1924
01:22:30,767 --> 01:22:33,633
You look like a man
who likes his trinkets.

1925
01:22:33,633 --> 01:22:35,167
- Adult trinkets.

1926
01:22:35,167 --> 01:22:38,633
- As it happens I own a small
trinket stand across the way.

1927
01:22:38,633 --> 01:22:40,967
- I'll give you a
cookie if you shut up.

1928
01:22:40,967 --> 01:22:43,833
- Oh, it's no use.

1929
01:22:43,833 --> 01:22:45,300
- Well, you never know.

1930
01:22:45,300 --> 01:22:46,400
Got a lot of stuff.

1931
01:22:46,400 --> 01:22:48,067
- Mostly Ringo hats.

1932
01:22:49,067 --> 01:22:51,667
- Well, no, no, no, no.

1933
01:22:51,667 --> 01:22:54,067
It's my monkey. I've
looked everywhere.

1934
01:22:54,067 --> 01:22:55,867
I just can't find it.

1935
01:22:55,867 --> 01:22:57,400
- You've lost a monkey?

1936
01:22:57,400 --> 01:22:58,700
- Check under your robe?

1937
01:22:58,700 --> 01:23:00,733
- What, a chimpanzee
from your show?

1938
01:23:00,733 --> 01:23:02,500
- No, a toy monkey.

1939
01:23:02,500 --> 01:23:03,900
- A toy monkey?

1940
01:23:03,900 --> 01:23:05,133
- Mm-hmm.

1941
01:23:05,133 --> 01:23:07,267
- You mean, the kind
with the cymbals?

1942
01:23:07,267 --> 01:23:08,200
- You've seen it?

1943
01:23:08,200 --> 01:23:09,033
- That's the damnedest thing.

1944
01:23:09,033 --> 01:23:10,267
- Yep, sure is.

1945
01:23:10,267 --> 01:23:12,567
- This morning,
some bum walks up.

1946
01:23:12,567 --> 01:23:15,000
Says for a dollar, he'll
give me this toy monkey.

1947
01:23:15,000 --> 01:23:17,933
You know, like the one
you're looking for,

1948
01:23:17,933 --> 01:23:18,767
so I said okay.

1949
01:23:18,767 --> 01:23:19,800
- Right, right.

1950
01:23:19,800 --> 01:23:20,967
Let's move on.

1951
01:23:20,967 --> 01:23:22,233
- You've got it?

1952
01:23:22,233 --> 01:23:23,433
- You're not gonna believe this.

1953
01:23:23,433 --> 01:23:24,933
- No, I'm not.

1954
01:23:24,933 --> 01:23:26,200
- Not an hour ago, an old
lady pulls up in a car.

1955
01:23:26,200 --> 01:23:27,133
- No!

1956
01:23:27,133 --> 01:23:28,167
- Offers me 20 buck for it.

1957
01:23:28,167 --> 01:23:30,133
20 bucks, I couldn't believe it!

1958
01:23:30,133 --> 01:23:31,267
- Yeah, me neither.

1959
01:23:31,267 --> 01:23:32,767
- You sold it to her?

1960
01:23:32,767 --> 01:23:35,833
- Damn right, would've given
her half my cart for 20 bucks.

1961
01:23:35,833 --> 01:23:38,000
- By the way, get
a haircut, hippie.

1962
01:23:38,000 --> 01:23:41,933
- Did you get her name or
where she lives, anything?

1963
01:23:41,933 --> 01:23:44,467
- Well, actually, I
keep a full dossier

1964
01:23:44,467 --> 01:23:46,100
on evil monkey buyers.

1965
01:23:46,100 --> 01:23:50,033
Her name's Mary Andrews.

1966
01:23:50,033 --> 01:23:53,600
312 Maple Drive.

1967
01:23:53,600 --> 01:23:56,667
Granted, I don't usually
accept checks, but she looked

1968
01:23:56,667 --> 01:23:58,600
respectable enough.

1969
01:23:58,600 --> 01:24:00,600
- Ride, Shadowfax, ride!

1970
01:24:00,600 --> 01:24:02,767
♪ Rock and roll truck ♪

1971
